<figure class="cache-figure" data-maintenance-chunks>
 <p class="figure-title">Smaller operations let other requests take a turn</p>
 <label>Items per operation <select data-chunk aria-label="Maintenance chunk size"><option value="12">12 · one long operation</option><option value="3">3 · four chunks</option><option value="1">1 · twelve chunks</option></select></label>
 <p class="figure-note">Three reads arrive at 2, 6 and 10 ms. Maintenance costs 12 ms in total; every read costs 1 ms.</p>
 <div class="maintenance-lane" data-lane aria-label="Server execution timeline"></div>
 <div class="memory-encoding-axis"><span>0 ms</span><span>15 ms</span></div>
 <p class="figure-note">Outlined blocks: maintenance · solid blocks: reads A, B and C</p>
 <div class="maintenance-readers">{['A','B','C'].map((name,i)=><div><small>Read {name}</small><strong data-wait={i}></strong><span data-start={i}></span></div>)}</div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>At each operation boundary, this illustrative scheduler serves waiting reads before continuing maintenance. Redis does not promise this priority or the displayed timings. Fixed chunk sizes here show the scheduling opportunity; SCAN COUNT is only a hint and does not guarantee a batch size or strict latency bound. Network and per-command overhead are omitted.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import {maintenanceSchedule} from '../../lib/caching/memory.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-maintenance-chunks]').forEach(root=>{const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-chunk]')!;const render=()=>{const s=maintenanceSchedule(Number(select.value));root.querySelector('[data-lane]')!.replaceChildren(...s.events.map(e=>{const block=document.createElement('span');block.className=e.type==='read'?'maintenance-read':'maintenance-work';block.style.left=`${e.start/15*100}%`;block.style.width=`${(e.end-e.start)/15*100}%`;block.textContent=e.type==='read'?String.fromCharCode(65+e.id):'';block.setAttribute('role','img');block.setAttribute('aria-label',`${e.type==='read'?`Read ${String.fromCharCode(65+e.id)}`:`Maintenance of ${e.count} items`}: ${e.start} to ${e.end} milliseconds`);return block;}));s.reads.forEach((r,i)=>{root.querySelector(`[data-wait="${i}"]`)!.textContent=`${r.start-r.arrive} ms wait`;root.querySelector(`[data-start="${i}"]`)!.textContent=`executes at ${r.start} ms`;});root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=`Maintenance still consumes 12 ms. Read A waits ${s.reads[0].start-2} ms. Splitting the work changes who waits, even though all work still finishes at ${s.end} ms in this model.`;};select.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
